doc:Factstitle_1 None:has_text_value "Nevertheless, the predictive accuracy of these methods is strongly conditioned by data quality and coverage and is often unsupported by a firm theoretical foundation. Hybrid approaches seek to improve predictive performance by combining physical theory with the adaptability of machine learning models. To address these limitations, this study proposes a GMA model that integrates a GRU with attention mechanisms, with the objective of achieving accurate RUL prediction for PEMFC." .
_:cf23367cb89c9e3a65781a23020deafa rdf:reifies <<( doc:Factstitle_1 None:has_text_value "Nevertheless, the predictive accuracy of these methods is strongly conditioned by data quality and coverage and is often unsupported by a firm theoretical foundation. Hybrid approaches seek to improve predictive performance by combining physical theory with the adaptability of machine learning models. To address these limitations, this study proposes a GMA model that integrates a GRU with attention mechanisms, with the objective of achieving accurate RUL prediction for PEMFC." )>> ;
